# Magic Scarf — Product / Implementation Notes

## Business architecture preserved

The rebuild does not alter the customer's category tree, product taxonomy, or B2B onboarding flow. Implementation follows what's already on the live site.

### Channel model

Magic Scarf operates two wholesale channels in parallel:

1. **Direct wholesale at magicscarf.com** — login-gated pricing, 50%-off-first-order incentive, half-price shipping, regional trade-show schedule.
2. **Faire reseller channel** — Net-60, free returns on first order, single-login convenience.

The rebuild preserves both channels. Faire is featured in (a) the home-page Faire band, (b) a dedicated `/faire` view, and (c) the footer Shop column. Customers logging in directly should still be encouraged toward direct (better margin); shoppers without a wholesale account should be routed toward Faire as a low-friction entry.

### Audience tiers

Wholesale registration captures **Type of Business** and **Annual Sales** at signup (verbatim from audited form):

| Business type | Annual sales tiers |
|---|---|
| Boutique · Clothing Store · Gift Shop | Under $250K → over $4M |
| Retail Shows · Mall Cart/Kiosk · Home Parties | (smaller-volume) |
| Multi-Location Retail · Wholesale Distributor · Other | (larger-volume) |

This data drives downstream tier-pricing and credit-limit decisions in the ERP. Tier assignment should remain manual at first (Magic Scarf staff approve every wholesale application within 1 business day per the audit).

## Merchandising flows

### Product card (PLP)
- Image + SKU eyebrow + title + category + variant-color chips (+N more) + "Sign in for price" lock + add-to-cart button
- Hover state: "Quick view →" pill at bottom (touch devices show it always)
- Heart/favorite button (top-right of image)
- Top-left badges: New / Best Seller / Heritage / Low Stock / 10% Off (audit-derived from the live site's "Now 10% Off" + "LOW STOCK" labels on Best Picks)

### PLP filters
| Group | Source |
|---|---|
| Subcategory | `SUBCATS[<parent>]` — audited (e.g. Ponchos has 5 subs: Lightweight / Button / Dress / Autumn-Winter / Faux Fur) |
| Color | 8-swatch row (Black / White / Wine / Navy / Gold / Sage / Terracotta / Blush) |
| Material | Cashmere Feel / Pashmina / Silk Blend / Sueded Cloth / Velvet |
| Pattern | Solid / Floral / Geometric / Animal Print / Paisley |
| In stock | Available now / Pre-order |

Sort options: Best sellers · New arrivals · Name A–Z · Recently restocked.

### PDP (Product Detail)

Layout: gallery left (sticky) + info right.

**Gallery:** main image + 4-thumb strip below + 47-color variant grid (auto-fill, scrollable to max-height 280px).

**Info column order (verbatim from WizCommerce older-B2B PDP standard):**
1. Breadcrumbs
2. SKU eyebrow + Spec sheet download link
3. Product H1
4. Category breadcrumb micro-line
5. Stock pill ("In stock · Ready to ship in 24h" or "Low stock · Order soon")
6. Description (verbatim from audited live PDP where harvested — e.g. for SKU 8672: "Perfect for all seasons. Soft and Comfortable. Versatility at its Best. Dress Up or Down. One Size Fits Most. 40″ from shoulder to point. 100% Acrylic. Imported.")
7. Color variant grid with named labels (47 colors for ponchos; smaller arrays for other categories)
8. Sourcing strip — Case-pack 6, MOQ 2 cases, Ships in 24h
9. Login-gated price box ("🔒 Sign in to view")
10. CTA: Sign in to View Price → after login → Add to Cart → after add → Quantity Stepper
11. Trust strip — Half-price shipping / Trade only / Net-30 terms / Ships in 24h
12. 4 accordions — Product Details · Specifications · Shipping & Returns · Care Instructions
13. Related Products (always-fills-to-4 — same category first, fallback to other cats)

### B2B workflow notes

- **Login-gated pricing** is enforced everywhere prices appear (PLP cards, PDP price box, cart summary, account orders). No prices are ever fabricated in the markup.
- **Add-to-Cart state machine**: Login → Add to Cart → Quantity Stepper. While logged out, the Add button opens the login modal.
- **Case-pack 6** is the WizCommerce default for this catalog. Customer should confirm per-category pack sizes (vests, hats and brooches likely differ).
- **MOQ 2 cases (12 units)** is the default. Confirm.
- **Net-30 terms** language is shown as "available on approved accounts" — the actual approval flow stays in the ERP.

